<Base title="How to use" description="How to consume key-atoms for signature verification across the *-atoms ecosystem.">
  <h1>How to use key-atoms</h1>

  <h2>Read the catalog over HTTPS</h2>
  <p>Every artifact is served under stable URLs with correct content-types:</p>
  <pre><code>curl https://key-atoms.com/exports/catalog.json
curl https://key-atoms.com/atoms/key/&lt;key-id&gt;.json
curl https://key-atoms.com/atoms/succession/&lt;succession-id&gt;.json
curl https://key-atoms.com/atoms/revocation/&lt;revocation-id&gt;.json</code></pre>

  <h2>Resolve a key by its <code>signer_key_id</code></h2>
  <p>Every <code>[[signatures]]</code> entry on any atom in the federation
  carries a <code>signer_key_id</code>. To verify, fetch the corresponding
  key atom from key-atoms, walk <code>succeeded_by</code> if present (the
  current authoritative key for a role lives at the end of the chain),
  check that the key is not revoked, and verify the signature with the
  declared algorithm.</p>

  <pre><code>{`// pseudo-code
const sig = atom.signatures[0];                          // { algorithm, signer_role, signer_key_id, signature, signed_at, covers }
let keyAtom = await fetch(\`/atoms/key/\${sig.signer_key_id}.json\`).then(r => r.json());
while (keyAtom.key.succeeded_by) {
  keyAtom = await fetch(\`/atoms/key/\${keyAtom.key.succeeded_by}.json\`).then(r => r.json());
}
const revoked = await fetch(\`/atoms/revocation/\${keyAtom.key.key_id}.json\`)
  .then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : null);
if (revoked) throw new Error("key revoked");
verifySignature(sig.algorithm, keyAtom.key.public_key, atom.content_hash, sig.signature);`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Trust model</h2>
  <p>See <a href="https://github.com/convergent-systems-co/atoms-spec">atoms-spec</a>,
  Part IV ("Signing and trust") for the full model: supported algorithms,
  signer roles, quorum semantics, and the Phase 2 governance escalation that
  applies specifically to this catalog.</p>

  <h2>Bootstrap status</h2>
  <p>This catalog is in <code>lifecycle: bootstrap</code> as of v1.1.0. The
  ML-DSA-65 root key atom has not yet been published. Until that atom
  lands, no v1.1.0 atom in the federation can be verified end-to-end. Ed25519
  v1.0.0 atoms remain verifiable against the legacy Ed25519 root if your
  consumer still resolves that key.</p>
</Base>
